 "reduction": "If x covers, the all-zero target is covered by some window j of weight <= R; rotating x to start at j preserves the multiset of cyclic windows, hence covering, and makes window 0 light. So every rotation class of covering sequences contains a string whose window 0 has weight <= R; the program enumerates exactly those strings (L>=n: window 0 over ball(0,R) times all 2^(L-n) suffixes; L<n: all 2^L strings filtered). Acceptance scans all 2^n targets. Independent of both worker implementations (all-strings brute force and FKM necklaces).",
